    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nI have a helpful git alias.\n\n```\n[alias]\n    git = !git\n```\n\nThis lets me get away with accidentally typing git multiple types.\n\n```console\n$ git git git --version\ngit version 2.55.0\n```\n\nHowever, when I use the `Git` command provided by mini.git, I noticed that it often presents the git output as a message or notification rather than a minigit buffer. This breaks the workflow I am attempting to set up for digging through logs and reviewing code with `Git log` and `Git diff`, etc. When I unset the alias, the output is sent to a minigit buffer as expected.\n\nThank you for creating and maintaining these excellent plugins!\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n    require('mini.git').setup()\n    require('mini.notify').setup() -- optional: makes the issue more noticable\n    ```\n\n3. Run `git config alias.git '!git'`.\n\n4. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n5. Run `Git help` and observe that a message/notification appears rather than a minigit buffer.\n\n6. Run `git config unset alias.git` and repeat steps four and five and observe that the output appears in a minigit buffer as expected.",
