            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I tried some things after creating this issue and figured out that doing this works:\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"mini.git\").setup({\n    job = { git_executable = vim.fn.exepath(\"git\") },\n})\n```\n\nPerhaps `vim.fn.exepath('git')` should be the default `git_executable` rather than just `'git'`? I'm not super familiar with how mini.git works, but it seems like it could be a more robust default independent of admittedly niche use case.",
