            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I tried some things after creating this issue and figured out that doing this works:\n> \n> require(\"mini.git\").setup({\n>     job = { git_executable = vim.fn.exepath(\"git\") },\n> })\n> \n> Perhaps `vim.fn.exepath('git')` should be the default `git_executable` rather than just `'git'`? I'm not super familiar with how mini.git works, but it seems like it could be a more robust default independent of admittedly niche use case.\n\nThat's a very nice find! Thanks for sharing, as it probably would have been a long time for me to find.\n\nUsing `vim.fn.exepath('git')` directly as default config value doesn't feel like a clean solution. As there are some subtle inconsistencies in how `config.job.git_executable` is used (which I noticed just now), I'll take a bit more time to find the most suitable solution here. Especially as there is a workaround to use in the meantime.",
